 = null when the demo member is not promoted. When no other member holds a Booked place and nobody is waiting, the counts stay unchanged.","A Booked or Waitlisted record on a studio-cancelled session is reported with status and badge 'Cancelled by studio' and appears in the Past list. Waitlisted records whose class has ended appear in neither list. All Cancelled records appear in Past, whatever their class time.","Duplicate-booking protection is the already_booked check inside the same request or transaction. No unique index or locking is added (ASM-8, ASM-16).","Build-time OpenAPI generation is detected when the app runs under the GetDocument.Insider tool, so startup database work can be skipped."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"0 of all error responses produced by the acceptance tests contain an exception type name or a stack-trace line; 100% have a code from the 13-value enum","text":"Error responses never expose raw server errors: every non-2xx response body is a contract Error with a code from the enum and a plain message."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"p95 latency ≤ 300 ms over 100 sequential GET /api/schedule calls against the seeded SQLite file on a developer machine","text":"GET /schedule on the seeded database answers quickly enough for the web app's 1-second render target."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"≥ 8 rule tests, one per §10 bullet, with a 100% pass rate in dotnet test","text":"App.Tests contains automated business-rule tests run through WebApplicationFactory with a fake TimeProvider, covering the §10 list: booking with spots, full plus waitlist join, promotion on cancel, booking window, late-cancel flag, overlap, 10-booking limit, and past/studio-cancelled rejection."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"20 sequential identical POST /bookings calls for one session leave exactly 1 non-cancelled booking row; 19 responses have status 409 already_booked","text":"Repeated Book taps do not create duplicate bookings."}],"outOfScope":["Web screens, design system, dark mode, motion and accessibility work: the web app is built in its own repo (request)","The end-to-end test (schedule → filter → book → My Bookings → cancel), which belongs to the web repo (ASM-9)","Seeding 40+ sessions over two weeks with 5 instructors as described in §4.3; only a few rows are seeded (Q-8)","Editing contracts/openapi.yaml, including its description that mentions local storage (ASM-10)","Sign-in, sign-up, payments, credits, membership management, staff/admin screens, notifications, calendar export, multiple locations, native apps and multi-language support (§12)","Making rule numbers (7 days, 15 minutes, 2 hours, 5 seconds, limit 10) or the demo member configurable; they stay code constants (ASM-6, ASM-13)","Changing the existing GET / \"API is up\" route, which stays as it is and stays out of the OpenAPI document (ASM-2, ASM-12)"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"The solution has been built, which writes App.Api/openapi/built","id":"AC-1.1","level":"job","then":"The comparison reports 0 differences in paths, methods, operationIds, parameters, request bodies, response status codes, schemas and the server url /api","when":"The factory's contract comparison job compares the built document with contracts/openapi.yaml"},{"given":"The API is running on seeded data","id":"AC-1.2","level":"api","then":"Every response status is one of the statuses the contract declares for that operation, and no call returns 404 for an unmapped route or 405","when":"Each of the 13 contract operations is called once with a valid request"}],"anchors":[{"lineEnd":8,"lineStart":6,"path":"App.Api/App.Api.csproj","quote":"    <!-- the build writes the API's OpenAPI document here; the factory compares it with contracts/openapi.yaml -->\n    <OpenApiDocumentsDirectory>$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)/openapi</OpenApiDocumentsDirectory>\n    <OpenApiGenerateDocumentsOptions>--file-name built</OpenApiGenerateDocumentsOptions>"}],"ears":"The API shall implement all 13 operations of contracts/