uated in this order: studio-cancelled → disabled; demo member holds a Booked/Waitlisted record → booked/waitlisted; started → disabled; outside booking window → disabled; full → join_waitlist; otherwise book. skipReason is always null because promotion never skips (ASM-5, ASM-15).","The cancel confirmation message uses \"today HH:mm\" when the class is on the current London day and \"ddd HH:mm\" otherwise. All times in messages are 24-hour Europe/London. startsAt/endsAt are serialised as UTC ISO-8601.","DaySummary.hasSessions ignores the type/intensity/timeOfDay filters.","currentStreakWeeks counts back from the current London week. If the current week has no Attended booking yet, counting starts from the previous week instead of returning 0.","A Booked record counts as upcoming until its session ends. Once the session ends it is reported as Attended in the past list (Q-2). While the session is in progress the record is still upcoming, with canChange=false.","Other members' booked places and waitlist places are stored as counts on the session (Q-4). The demo member's waitlist position is stored on their booking row. Promotion notices are stored as promoted-at and notice-acknowledged fields on the booking (Q-7).","Rule tests run against a temporary SQLite file through WebApplicationFactory, and the fake TimeProvider is injected (ASM-9, ASM-14). Tests may insert session and booking rows directly to set up a state."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"0 of all 4xx/5xx responses produced by the rule test suite contain the text \"Exception\" or a line starting with \"   at \"","text":"Error responses never expose raw server errors or stack traces."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"10 back-to-back POST /api/bookings calls for the same session leave exactly 1 non-cancelled booking row for that session (1 response 201, 9 responses 409 already_booked)","text":"Repeated Book taps do not create duplicate bookings."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"p95 latency of GET /api/schedule is 200 ms or le