DED","sources":["I-1","ASM-1","ASM-2","ASM-10","ASM-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API is running","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the body fields are id=1, name=\"Alex Rivera\", initials=\"AR\", membership=\"Unlimited Monthly\"","when":"A client sends GET /api/me"}],"ears":"When a client requests GET /me, the API shall return status 200 with the demo member id 1, name \"Alex Rivera\", initials \"AR\" and membership \"Unlimited Monthly\".","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-6","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The clock is set to 2026-10-14T09:00:00Z (Wed 10:00 London) and sessions exist on 2026-10-14 at 07:00Z and 11:15Z and none on 2026-10-18","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 with today=\"2026-10-14\", date=\"2026-10-14\", weekStart=\"2026-10-12\", canGoPreviousWeek=false, canGoNextWeek=true, a days list of 7 entries where days[0].label=\"Mon 12\", only the 2026-10-14 entry has isToday=true, the 2026-10-18 entry has hasSessions=false, and the sessions list is ordered by startsAt ascending","when":"A client sends GET /api/schedule with no query"},{"given":"The clock is set to 2026-10-14T09:00:00Z","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 with weekStart=\"2026-10-19\", canGoPreviousWeek=true and canGoNextWeek=false","when":"A client sends GET /api/schedule?date=2026-10-21"},{"given":"The clock is set to 2026-10-14T09:00:00Z","id":"AC-4.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 and the error code field is invalid_request","when":"A client sends GET /api/schedule?date=2026-10-05 or GET /api/schedule?date=2026-10-26"}],"ears":"When a client requests GET /schedule, the API shall return the Monday-to-Sunday Europe/London week that contains the selected date (default today), with 7 day summaries labelled like \"Mon 12\", the isToday and hasSessions flags, canGoPreviousWeek and canGoNextWeek, and the selected day's sessions ordered by start time.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","ASM-7","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"On 2026-10-14 there are a Yoga Low session at 07:00 London, a Pilates Medium session at 12:00 London, and a Boxing Medium session at 17:00 London","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"The returned sessions list contains only the Yoga and Boxing sessions","when":"A client sends GET /api/schedule?date=2026-10-14&type=Yoga&type=Boxing"},{"given":"The same three sessions","id":"AC-5.2","level":"api","then":"The returned sessions list contains only the session starting at 12:00 London","when":"A client sends GET /api/schedule?date=2026-10-14&timeOfDay=Afternoon"},{"given":"The same three sessions","id":"AC-5.3","level":"api","then":"The returned sessions list contains only the Boxing session starting at 17:00 London","when":"A client sends GET /api/schedule?date=2026-10-14&timeOfDay=Evening&intensity=Medium"},{"given":"The same three sessions","id":"AC-5.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 and the error code field is invalid_request","when":"A client sends GET /api/schedule?date=2026-10-14&type=Zumba"}],"ears":"When GET /schedule includes type, intensity or timeOfDay values, the API shall return only the selected day's sessions that match any listed value of each given filter and all given filters together, where Morning is a London start before 12:00, Afternoon is 12:00–16:59 and Evening is 17:00 or later.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Scheduled session has capacity 20 and 14 booked","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"The response fields are availabilityLabel=\"6 spots left\" and capacityLabel=\"6 of 20 spots left\"","when":"A client sends GET /api/sessions/{id}"},{"given":"Scheduled sessions with capacity 12 and 10 booked, and with capacity 12 and 11 booked","id":"AC-6.2","level":"api","then":"The availabilityLabel values returned are \"Only 2 left\" and \"1 spot left\"","when":"A client sends GET /api/sessions/{id} for each"},{"given":"A Scheduled session has capacity 16, 16 booked by other members and 3 others on the waitlist","id":"AC-6.3","level":"api","then":"The response fields are bookedCount=16, waitlistCount=3, availabilityLabel=\"Full · 3 on waitlist\", capacityLabel=\"0 of 16 spots left\"","when":"A client sends GET /api/sessions/{id}"},{"given":"A session has status Cancelled by studio","id":"AC-6.4","level":"api","then":"The response fields are status=\"Cancelled by studio\" and availabilityLabel=\"Cancelled\"","when":"A client sends GET /api/sessions/{id}"}],"ears":"The API shall return each Session with bookedCount and waitlistCount covering both the demo member and the other members, capacityLabel \"{spotsLeft} of {capacity} spots left\", and availabilityLabel \"Cancelled\" for studio-cancelled sessions, \"Full · {waitlistCount} on waitlist\" when full, \"1 spot left\" for 1 spot, \"Only {n} left\" for 2–3 spots and \"{n} spots left\" for more than 3 spots.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-14T09:00:00Z and a Scheduled session starting 2026-10-14T10:30:00Z has capacity 20 and the demo member holds Booked booking 501 on it","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"The response actionState is kind=booked, canChange=true, bookingId=501, lateCancellation=true, and myBookingId=501","when":"A client sends GET /api/sessions/{id}"},{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-14T09:00:00Z and a full session starting tomorrow has 3 others on the waitlist and no demo record","id":"AC-7.2","level":"api","then":"The response actionState is kind=join_waitlist with position=4 and myBookingId is null","when":"A client sends GET /api/sessions/{id}"},{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-14T09:00:00Z and the demo member holds no record on three Scheduled sessions starting 2026-10-14T08:30:00Z, 2026-10-21T09:01:00Z and 2026-10-14T09:10:00Z","id":"AC-7.3","level":"api","then":"Each response actionState is kind=disabled, canChange=false, with reason values \"Class has started\", \"Booking opens 7 days before class\" and \"Booking closes 15 minutes before class\" respectively","when":"A client sends GET /api/sessions/{id} for each"},{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-14T09:00:00Z and a Scheduled session starting tomorrow has capacity 12 and 10 booked with no demo record","id":"AC-7.4","level":"api","then":"The response actionState is kind=book with spotsLeft=2","when":"A client sends GET /api/sessions/{id}"},{"given":"The demo member holds Waitlisted booking 502 at position 2 on a session starting tomorrow","id":"AC-7.5","level":"api","then":"The response actionState is kind=waitlisted, position=2, bookingId=502, canChange=true","when":"A client sends GET /api/sessions/{id}"}],"ears":"The API shall return each Session with an actionState and myBookingId for the demo member: disabled with reason \"Cancelled by studio\" for studio-cancelled sessions; booked or waitlisted (with bookingId, position, canChange false once started, and lateCancellation true when under 2 hours to start) when the member holds such a record; otherwise disabled with reason \"Class has started\", \"Booking opens 7 days before class\" or \"Booking closes 15 minutes before class\"; otherwise join_waitlist with position waitlistCount+1 when full, or book with spotsLeft.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","ASM-7","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"No session with id 99999 exists","id":"AC-8.1","level":"api","then":"Each response status is 404 and the error code field is not_found","when":"A client sends GET /api/sessions/99999, POST /api/bookings {\"sessionId\":99999}, POST /api/waitlist {\"sessionId\":99999} or POST /api/test/sessions/99999/simulate-other-member-cancellation"},{"given":"No booking with id 99999 exists","id":"AC-8.2","level":"api","then":"Each response status is 404 and the error code field is not_found","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings/99999/undo, /cancel or /leave-waitlist"}],"ears":"If a request names a session id or booking id that does not exist, then the API shall return status 404 with error code not_found.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-14T09:00:00Z and \"Reformer Core\" starts 2026-10-15T08:30:00Z with capacity 12 and 10 booked","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201, booking.status=\"Booked\", booking.lateCancel=false, session.bookedCount=11, session.availabilityLabel=\"1 spot left\", session.actionState.kind=\"booked\", and message=\"You're booked for Reformer Core · Thu 09:30\"","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings {\"sessionId\":<id>}"},{"given":"The booking from AC-9.1 was created","id":"AC-9.2","level":"api","then":"Exactly one row for that session has status Booked with the returned booking id","when":"The test reads the bookings table in SQLite"}],"ears":"When a client posts a bookable session to POST /bookings, the API shall store a new Booked booking row for the demo member and return status 201 with the booking, the refreshed session and the message \"You're booked for {name} · {ddd HH:mm London}\".","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-2","I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-14T09:00:00Z and a session starting tomorrow has capacity 16 and 16 booked","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409, the error code is class_full, the error session field has actionState.kind=\"join_waitlist\", and the booking row count is unchanged","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings for it"},{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-14T09:00:00Z","id":"AC-10.2","level":"api","then":"The response statuses are 201, 409 outside_booking_window, 201 and 409 outside_booking_window respectively","when":"A client books sessions starting at 2026-10-21T09:00:00Z, 2026-10-21T09:01:00Z, 2026-10-14T09:15:00Z and 2026-10-14T09:14:00Z"},{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-14T09:00:00Z and one session started at 08:30Z and another is Cancelled by studio","id":"AC-10.3","level":"api","then":"The response statuses are 409 with error code class_has_started and cancelled_by_studio respectively","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings for each"},{"given":"The demo member already holds a Booked record on a session","id":"AC-10.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code already_booked and the count of non-cancelled rows for that session stays 1","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings for the same session"},{"given":"The demo member cancelled their booking on a session that is still bookable","id":"AC-10.5","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and the bookings table holds two rows for that session: the old Cancelled row and a new Booked row with a different id","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings for the same session"}],"ears":"If POST /bookings targets a session that is cancelled by the studio, has started, is more than 7 days or less than 15 minutes from start, already has a Booked or Waitlisted record for the demo member, or is at capacity, then the API shall return status 409 with error code cancelled_by_studio, class_has_started, outside_booking_window, already_booked or class_full respectively and store no new booking row, including the refreshed session in the error only for class_full.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","Q-6","ASM-8","ASM-16"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The demo member is Booked on \"Power HIIT\" from 2026-10-15T17:00:00Z to 17:45:00Z (18:00–18:45 London)","id":"AC-11.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409, the error code is overlap and the message is \"You're already booked for Power HIIT at 18:00–18:45.\"","when":"A client books a Spin session starting 2026-10-15T17:30:00Z"},{"given":"The same Power HIIT booking","id":"AC-11.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201","when":"A client books a session starting exactly 2026-10-15T17:45:00Z"},{"given":"The demo member is only Waitlisted on a session from 17:00Z to 17:45Z","id":"AC-11.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201","when":"A client books a session starting 17:30Z the same day"}],"ears":"If POST /bookings targets a session whose time range overlaps a session where the demo member holds a Booked record, then the API shall return status 409 with error code overlap and the message \"You're already booked for {name} at {HH:mm}–{HH:mm}.\" in London time.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The demo member holds 10 Booked records on non-overlapping sessions that have not started","id":"AC-12.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409, the error code is limit_reached and the message is \"You've reached the limit of 10 upcoming classes.\"","when":"A client books an 11th non-overlapping bookable session"},{"given":"The demo member holds 9 upcoming Booked records, 2 Waitlisted records and 3 past Attended bookings","id":"AC-12.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201","when":"A client books another non-overlapping bookable session"}],"ears":"If the demo member already holds 10 Booked records on sessions that have not started, then the API shall reject POST /bookings with status 409, error code limit_reached and the message \"You've reached the limit of 10 upcoming classes.\"","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-6","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Booking 503 on \"Reformer Core\" was created at T and the clock is T+4s","id":"AC-13.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, message=\"Booking undone — Reformer Core\", session.bookedCount is back to its value before booking, session.myBookingId is null, and no row with id 503 remains in the bookings table","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings/503/undo"},{"given":"Booking 503 was created at T and the clock is T+6s","id":"AC-13.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code undo_expired and row 503 still has status Booked","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings/503/undo"},{"given":"Booking 507 is Waitlisted or Cancelled and was created 1 second ago","id":"AC-13.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code invalid_booking_state","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings/507/undo"}],"ears":"When a client posts POST /bookings/{bookingId}/undo for a Booked record created 5 seconds ago or less, the API shall delete that booking row and return status 200 with the refreshed session and the message \"Booking undone — {name}\".","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-14T16:30:00Z and the demo member's Booked record 506 is on \"Power Spin\" starting 2026-10-14T18:00:00Z (90 minutes away)","id":"AC-14.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, booking.status=\"Cancelled\", booking.lateCancel=true, booking.cancelledAt=\"2026-10-14T16:30:00Z\", and message=\"Booking cancelled — Power Spin, today 19:00\"","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings/506/cancel"},{"given":"The demo member's Booked record is on a session starting exactly 2 hours from now","id":"AC-14.2","level":"api","then":"The response field booking.lateCancel is false","when":"A client cancels it"},{"given":"The demo member's Booked record is on a session that started 5 minutes ago","id":"AC-14.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code class_has_started and the row status is still Booked","when":"A client cancels it"},{"given":"Booking 504 is Waitlisted","id":"AC-14.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code invalid_booking_state","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings/504/cancel"}],"ears":"When a client posts POST /bookings/{bookingId}/cancel for a Booked record whose session has not started, the API shall set the row to Cancelled with cancelledAt now and lateCancel true only when the session starts in less than 2 hours, and return status 200 with the booking, the refreshed session and a confirmation message.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A session has capacity 10, bookedCount 10 including the demo member's Booked record, and waitlistCount 2 (other members)","id":"AC-15.1","level":"api","then":"The response session fields are bookedCount=10 and waitlistCount=1","when":"A client cancels the demo member's booking"},{"given":"A session has capacity 10, bookedCount 10 including the demo member's Booked record, and waitlistCount 0","id":"AC-15.2","level":"api","then":"The response session fields are bookedCount=9 and waitlistCount=0","when":"A client cancels the demo member's booking"}],"ears":"When the demo member cancels a Booked record on a session with members on the waitlist, the API shall promote the first other member in line, so the returned session keeps the same bookedCount and its waitlistCount drops by 1.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-14T09:00:00Z and \"HIIT Blast\" starts 2026-10-15T11:15:00Z with capacity 16, 16 booked and 3 others waitlisted","id":"AC-16.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201, booking.status=\"Waitlisted\", booking.waitlistPosition=4, session.waitlistCount=4, session.actionState.kind=\"waitlisted\" and message=\"You're on the waitlist for HIIT Blast · Thu 12:15 — you're #4\"","when":"A client sends POST /api/waitlist {\"sessionId\":<id>}"},{"given":"A bookable session has 2 spots left","id":"AC-16.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code not_full","when":"A client sends POST /api/waitlist for it"},{"given":"The demo member already holds a Waitlisted record on a full session","id":"AC-16.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code already_booked","when":"A client sends POST /api/waitlist for it again"},{"given":"Full sessions that have started, are Cancelled by studio, and start more than 7 days from now","id":"AC-16.4","level":"api","then":"The response error codes are class_has_started, cancelled_by_studio and outside_booking_window respectively, each with status 409","when":"A client sends POST /api/waitlist for each"}],"ears":"When a client posts a full, bookable session to POST /waitlist, the API shall store a new Waitlisted row with waitlistPosition equal to the previous waitlistCount plus 1, and return status 201 with the booking, the refreshed session and the message \"You're on the waitlist for {name} · {ddd HH:mm London} — you're #{position}\"; otherwise it shall return 409 with already_booked, not_full, outside_booking_window, class_has_started or cancelled_by_studio.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","Q-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The demo member holds Waitlisted record 504 at position 2 on \"Vinyasa Flow\" (waitlistCount 3) starting 30 minutes from now","id":"AC-17.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, booking.status=\"Cancelled\", booking.lateCancel=false, booking.waitlistPosition=null, session.waitlistCount=2, and message=\"You've left the waitlist for Vinyasa Flow\"","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings/504/leave-waitlist"},{"given":"Booking 506 is Booked","id":"AC-17.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code invalid_booking_state","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings/506/leave-waitlist"},{"given":"The demo member's Waitlisted record is on a session that started 1 minute ago","id":"AC-17.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with error code class_has_started","when":"A client leaves the waitlist"}],"ears":"When a client posts POST /bookings/{bookingId}/leave-waitlist for a Waitlisted record whose session has not started, the API shall set the row to Cancelled with lateCancel false and waitlistPosition null, lower the session's waitlistCount by 1, and return status 200 with the message \"You've left the waitlist for {name}\".","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-14T09:00:00Z and the demo member holds Booked on a session today at 18:00Z, Waitlisted at position 2 tomorrow, and Booked on 2026-10-16","id":"AC-18.1","level":"api","then":"The response upcoming list has 3 groups labelled \"Today\", \"Tomorrow\" and \"Fri 16 Oct\", and the Waitlisted row has badge \"Waitlisted #2\" and waitlistPosition=2","when":"A client sends GET /api/me/bookings"},{"given":"The demo member holds a Booked record on a session that ended yesterday and a late-cancelled record from last week","id":"AC-18.2","level":"api","then":"The past list shows the ended booking first with status=\"Attended\", badge=\"Attended\", canChange=false, then the cancelled booking with badge=\"Late cancel\"; the stored row for the ended booking still has status Booked","when":"A client sends GET /api/me/bookings"},{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-14T16:30:00Z and the demo member is Booked on a session starting 18:00Z","id":"AC-18.3","level":"api","then":"That row has isLateIfCancelledNow=true and canChange=true","when":"A client sends GET /api/me/bookings"}],"ears":"When a client requests GET /me/bookings, the API shall return Booked and Waitlisted records whose sessions have not ended as upcoming groups by London day (labelled \"Today\", \"Tomorrow\" or \"ddd d MMM\") ordered by start time, and Cancelled and ended Booked records as the past list most recent first, reporting an ended Booked record as status and badge \"Attended\" without changing the stored row.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","Q-2","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-22T12:00:00Z; the demo member has 2 upcoming Booked records, 1 Waitlisted record, ended Booked records on 2026-10-06, 2026-10-13 and 2026-10-20, and one late-cancelled record on 2026-10-15","id":"AC-19.1","level":"api","then":"The response fields are upcoming=2, classesThisMonth=3, currentStreakWeeks=3","when":"A client sends GET /api/me/stats"},{"given":"The demo member has no Attended bookings","id":"AC-19.2","level":"api","then":"The response fields classesThisMonth and currentStreakWeeks are both 0","when":"A client sends GET /api/me/stats"}],"ears":"When a client requests GET /me/stats, the API shall return upcoming as the count of the demo member's Booked records on sessions that have not started, classesThisMonth as the count of Attended bookings in the current London calendar month, and currentStreakWeeks as the number of consecutive Monday-to-Sunday weeks with at least one Attended booking.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-2","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The demo member was promoted from the waitlist on \"Power Ride\" starting 2026-10-15T06:15:00Z","id":"AC-20.1","level":"api","then":"The response notices list holds 1 entry with that bookingId and message=\"Good news! You're off the waitlist and booked for Power Ride · Thu 07:15\"","when":"A client sends GET /api/me/promotion-notices"},{"given":"The notice from AC-20.1 is listed","id":"AC-20.2","level":"api","then":"The acknowledge response status is 204 with an empty body and the notices list returned afterwards is empty","when":"A client sends POST /api/me/promotion-notices/acknowledge and then GET /api/me/promotion-notices"}],"ears":"While a demo member booking has a promoted-at time and no acknowledgement, the API shall list it in GET /me/promotion-notices with bookingId, sessionId, sessionName, startsAt and the message \"Good news! You're off the waitlist and booked for {name} · {ddd HH:mm London}\".","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","Q-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A session has capacity 14, bookedCount 14 (all other members), and waitlistCount 1 which is the demo member's Waitlisted record 502 at position 1","id":"AC-21.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, booking.id=502, booking.status=\"Booked\", booking.waitlistPosition=null, session.bookedCount=14, session.waitlistCount=0, and GET /api/me/promotion-notices then lists booking 502","when":"A client sends POST /api/test/sessions/{id}/simulate-other-member-cancellation"},{"given":"A full session has waitlistCount 2: one other member first and the demo member at position 2","id":"AC-21.2","level":"api","then":"The response booking.status is \"Waitlisted\" with waitlistPosition=1, session.waitlistCount=1, session.bookedCount unchanged, and no promotion notice is listed","when":"A client calls the simulate endpoint for it"},{"given":"A session has bookedCount 8 (other members), waitlistCount 0 and no demo record","id":"AC-21.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, booking is null and session.bookedCount=7","when":"A client calls the simulate endpoint for it"},{"given":"The API runs in the Production environment","id":"AC-21.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, not 404","when":"A client calls the simulate endpoint for an existing session"}],"ears":"When a client posts POST /test/sessions/{sessionId}/simulate-other-member-cancellation, the API shall remove one other member's booked place and promote the first in line: the demo member to Booked with a promotion notice if they are first, otherwise one other waitlisted member (lowering waitlistCount and moving the demo member up one place), and return status 200 with the refreshed session and the demo member's booking on that session or null.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","Q-3","Q-4","Q-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The demo member holds 10 upcoming Booked records, one of which overlaps a full session where they are Waitlisted at position 1","id":"AC-22.1","level":"api","then":"The response booking.status is \"Booked\" and booking.skipReason is null, and GET /api/me/stats then returns upcoming=11","when":"A client calls the simulate endpoint for the full session"}],"ears":"When the demo member is promoted from a waitlist, the API shall make the record Booked even if it overlaps another Booked session or takes the member above 10 upcoming Booked records.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-5","ASM-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"No database file exists at the configured connection string","id":"AC-23.1","level":"api","then":"The schedule response for the seeding day or a later day this week has at least 1 session, the my-bookings response has at least 1 upcoming Booked row, at least 1 upcoming Waitlisted row on a full session, and at least 1 past Attended row, and the sessions table count is 15 or fewer","when":"The API starts and a client sends GET /api/schedule, GET /api/me/bookings and GET /api/me/stats"},{"given":"A seeded database where at least 1 session has status Cancelled by studio","id":"AC-23.2","level":"api","then":"At least 1 row has status Cancelled by studio and at least 1 row has booked count equal to capacity","when":"The test reads the sessions table"},{"given":"A database already holding sessions and a booking made through the API","id":"AC-23.3","level":"api","then":"The sessions row count is unchanged and GET /api/me/bookings still returns the booking made before the restart","when":"The API is restarted against the same file"},{"given":"A clean checkout with no database file","id":"AC-23.4","level":"job","then":"No database file is created at the configured path","when":"dotnet build runs and generates App.Api/openapi/built.json"}],"anchors":[{"lineEnd":6,"lineStart":5,"path":"App.Api/Program.cs","quote":"builder.Services.AddOpenApi();\n// a local file database; nothing touches it at startup (the build runs this file to write the API's OpenAPI document)"}],"ears":"When the API starts with a SQLite database that has no tables or no rows, the API shall create the schema with EnsureCreated and seed sample sessions dated relative to the seeding day in Europe/London plus demo member bookings, but it shall skip this when the process runs only to generate the OpenAPI document.","id":"REQ-23","op":"MODIFIED","sources":["I-2","Q-5","Q-8","ASM-3","ASM-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API runs with the App connection string pointing at a path it cannot open","id":"AC-24.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 500, the error code field is storage_failure, and the response body contains neither \"Exception\" nor a line starting with \"   at \"","when":"A client sends GET /api/me/bookings or POST /api/bookings"}],"ears":"If reading or writing the database fails or another exception is not handled, then the API shall return status 500 with error code storage_failure and a plain-language message, with no stack trace or exception details in the response.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API is running","id":"AC-25.1","level":"api","then":"Each response status is 400 and the error code field is invalid_request","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings with body {} and POST /api/waitlist with body \"not json\""}],"ears":"If a request body is malformed or misses sessionId, then the API shall return status 400 with error code invalid_request.","id":"REQ-25","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A WebApplicationFactory replaces TimeProvider with a fake clock set to 2026-10-14T23:30:00Z (00:30 on 15 Oct in London)","id":"AC-26.1","level":"api","then":"The response field today is \"2026-10-15\"","when":"A client sends GET /api/schedule"}],"ears":"The API shall read the current time for all time rules, labels and \"today\" from the TimeProvider registered in dependency injection, defaulting to the system clock.","id":"REQ-26","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-9","ASM-14"]}],"suggestions":["The contract has skipReason (overlap, limit_reached, outside_booking_window) on Booking and ActionState, which suggests promotion could be skipped. ASM-5/ASM-15 say promote anyway. Confirm with the product owner whether skipReason should ever be filled.","The contract's description still says it is served over local storage in the browser. Consider updating it in a future contract version, since this run uses SQLite.","Decide what availabilityLabel should say for a full session with an empty waitlist (\"Full\" vs \"Full · 0 on waitlist\"). The contract does not show this case.","Decide whether a Waitlisted record on a session that has ended should appear in the past list, be hidden, or be shown as Cancelled.","Consider limiting the /test simulate hook to non-production environments in a later release. Q-3 asked for it to be mapped in every environment for now.","For stronger protection against concurrent duplicate bookings, consider a unique partial index on (member, session) for non-cancelled rows."]},{"assumptions":["Endpoints are mapped at the contract paths (/me, …) with UsePathBase(\"/api\") so /api/me answers and the built document keeps contract paths with server /api (ASM-1). ASM-11 (an /api route group) conflicts with this; acceptance criteria call /api/... so they hold under either choice, but the built document must keep the contract's unprefixed paths.","Q-5 and Q-8 (seed a few rows at startup when the database is empty) replace ASM-3 ('the system starts empty').","Time comes from an injected TimeProvider (system clock by default). Tests use WebApplicationFactory with a fake clock and set up sessions/bookings by writing rows to the test SQLite database (ASM-9, ASM-14).","Booking window limits are inclusive: a class exactly 7×24 hours away or exactly 15 minutes away can be booked. Late cancellation means strictly less than 2 hours before start. Undo is allowed up to and including 5 seconds after createdAt.","Overlap uses half-open ranges [startsAt, endsAt): a class starting exactly when another ends does not overlap. Only Booked records for classes that have not ended count toward overlap and the 10-booking limit.","When several rejections apply, the order checked is: not_found, cancelled_by_studio, class_has_started, outside_booking_window, already_booked, then class_full/not_full, overlap, limit_reached.","bookedCount and waitlistCount in responses include the demo member. waitlistCount = anonymous waitlisted count plus 1 if the demo member is waitlisted (this matches the joinWaitlist example going from 3 to 4 at position 4).","Promotion ignores overlap and the 10-booking limit (ASM-5, ASM-15), so skipReason is always null in this release.","A booking held for a session the studio cancelled is reported with status/badge 'Cancelled by studio' and listed under past. Booked/Waitlisted records for classes that have started but not ended stay under upcoming with canChange false. Cancelled records are listed under past whatever their class date.","Streak counts back from the current London week; if the current week has no Attended record yet, counting starts from the previous week.","The availabilityLabel for a full session with no waitlist is not covered by the contract examples; the build may use 'Full · 0 on waitlist' and tests do not assert it."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"p95 latency of GET /api/schedule under 200 ms over 100 sequential requests on the seeded database on a developer machine","text":"Reads of the schedule against the seeded SQLite database respond quickly enough for the web app's 1-second render target."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"p95 latency under 300 ms over 100 sequential write requests on the seeded database","text":"Write operations (book, waitlist, cancel, leave, undo) respond within the budget that lets the web app reconcile its optimistic update."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"0 differences reported by the factory's comparison of App.Api/openapi/built.json against contracts/openapi.yaml on every build","text":"The generated OpenAPI document stays identical to the locked contract."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"0 responses with status ≥ 400 across the business-rule test suite whose body contains a stack trace, exception type name or SQL text","text":"No error response leaks internals."},{"id":"NFR-5","metric":"The App.Tests rule suite passes 10 out of 10 consecutive runs with a fake clock","text":"Business-rule tests are deterministic because time comes from an injected TimeProvider."}],"outOfScope":["Web screens, design system, dark mode, motion, responsive layout and accessibility (§6–§7); the web app is built in its own repo per the request","The end-to-end UI test (open schedule → filter → book → My Bookings → cancel); it belongs to the web repo (ASM-9)","Sign-in, sign-up, payments, credits, membership purchase (§12 of the request)","Staff/instructor/admin screens and schedule editing","Email, SMS and push notifications; promotion is announced only via the promotion-notices endpoints","Seeding 40+ sessions, 5 instructors and the full §4.3 data set; only a handful of rows are seeded (Q-8)","Editing the locked contract, including its 'served inside the browser over local storage' description (ASM-10)","Storing other members as individual records; they are represented only as counts on the session (Q-4)","Configurable rule values; the 7-day, 15-minute, 2-hour, 5-second and 10-booking values are code constants (ASM-6, ASM-13)"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API is running with the seeded database","id":"AC-1.1","level":"api","then":"Every response status is 200 and every response body is JSON that matches the contract schema for that operation","when":"A client sends GET /api/me, GET /api/schedule, GET /api/me/bookings, GET /api/me/stats and GET /api/me/promotion-notices"},{"given":"The API is running in the Production environment with the seeded database","id":"AC-1.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, not 404, so the test hook is mapped in every environment","when":"A client sends POST /api/test/sessions/{id}/simulate-other-member-cancellation for a seeded session id"},{"given":"The API is running","id":"AC-1.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the body is \"API is up\"","when":"A client sends GET /"}],"ears":"The Booking API shall answer every operation of contracts/openapi.yaml at the path \"/api\" followed by the contract path (for example GET /api/me, POST /api/bookings, POST /api/test/sessions/{sessionId}/simulate-other-member-cancellation), using the HTTP method the contract declares.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-1","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A clean checkout","id":"AC-2.1","level":"job","then":"The file App.Api/openapi/built.json is written; the factory's compare against contracts/openapi.yaml reports a count of 0 differences in operations, paths, parameters, response codes and schemas, and the servers list has the value \"/api\"","when":"dotnet build runs for App.Api"},{"given":"The generated file App.Api/openapi/built.json","id":"AC-2.2","level":"job","then":"The list has no entry for \"/\" and contains exactly getMember, getSchedule, getSession, createBooking, undoBooking, cancelBooking, joinWaitlist, leaveWaitlist, getMyBookings, getStats, listPromotionNotices, acknowledgePromotionNotices and simulateOtherMemberCancellation","when":"A test reads its paths list"}],"ears":"When the build generates the API's OpenAPI document into App.Api/openapi, the Booking API shall emit a document with the same 13 operationIds, paths, parameters, response status codes and component schemas as contracts/openapi.yaml, server url \"/api\", and no GET / operation.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-1","ASM-2","ASM-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API is running","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the body fields are id=1, name=\"Alex Rivera\", initials=\"AR\", membership=\"Unlimited Monthly\"","when":"A client sends GET /api/me"}],"ears":"When a client calls getMember, the Booking API shall return status 200 with the demo member id 1, name \"Alex Rivera\", initials \"AR\" and membership \"Unlimited Monthly\".","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The injected clock reads 2026-10-14 10:00 Europe/London, sessions exist on 2026-10-14 at 18:00, 07:00 and 12:30 London (one of them Cancelled by studio) and no session exists on 2026-10-18","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200; today and date are \"2026-10-14\", weekStart is \"2026-10-12\", canGoPreviousWeek is false, canGoNextWeek is true; the days list has 7 entries from \"Mon 12\" to \"Sun 18\" with isToday true only for 2026-10-14 and hasSessions false for 2026-10-18; the sessions list has 3 entries in the order 07:00, 12:30, 18:00 including the studio-cancelled one","when":"A client sends GET /api/schedule with no query"},{"given":"The injected clock reads 2026-10-14 10:00 Europe/London","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, weekStart is \"2026-10-19\", canGoPreviousWeek is true and canGoNextWeek is false","when":"A client sends GET /api/schedule?date=2026-10-21"}],"ears":"When a client calls getSchedule, the Booking API shall return the selected day (default today in Europe/London), today, the Monday weekStart of that week, seven day summaries Monday to Sunday labelled \"Ddd d\" with isToday and hasSessions, canGoPreviousWeek true only for the next week, canGoNextWeek true only for the current week, and that day's sessions ordered by start time including studio-cancelled ones.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","ASM-7","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"On the selected day there are a Yoga Low session at 07:00, a Yoga High session at 12:00, a Spin Low session at 17:00 and a Boxing Medium session at 16:59 (London)","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"The response sessions list contains exactly the 07:00 Yoga and the 17:00 Spin sessions","when":"A client sends GET /api/schedule?type=Yoga&type=Spin&intensity=Low"},{"given":"The same four sessions","id":"AC-5.2","level":"api","then":"The response sessions list contains exactly the 12:00 and 16:59 sessions","when":"A client sends GET /api/schedule?timeOfDay=Afternoon"},{"given":"The same four sessions","id":"AC-5.3","level":"api","then":"The response sessions list contains exactly the 17:00 session","when":"A client sends GET /api/schedule?timeOfDay=Evening"}],"ears":"When getSchedule receives type, intensity or timeOfDay query values, the Booking API shall return only sessions whose type is in the type list, whose intensity is in the intensity list and whose London start time falls in a listed time of day (Morning before 12:00, Afternoon 12:00 to 16:59, Evening from 17:00), ignoring any filter that is not supplied.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The injected clock reads 2026-10-14 10:00 Europe/London","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"Each response status is 400 and each body field code is \"invalid_request\" with a non-empty message","when":"A client sends GET /api/schedule?date=2026-10-26, then GET /api/schedule?date=2026-10-11, then GET /api/schedule?date=not-a-date, then GET /api/schedule?type=Zumba"}],"ears":"If getSchedule receives a malformed date, a date outside the current and next Europe/London week, or a filter value outside the contract enums, then the Booking API shall return status 400 with Error code \"invalid_request\".","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A session with id 210 exists with an instructor and two whatToBring items","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the body has id 210, the instructor object with id, name, bio and avatarUrl, and a whatToBring list with 2 items","when":"A client sends GET /api/sessions/210"},{"given":"No session with id 99999 exists","id":"AC-7.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 404 and the body field code is \"not_found\"","when":"A client sends GET /api/sessions/99999"}],"ears":"When a client calls getSession, the Booking API shall return status 200 with the session including instructor, whatToBring, counts, labels, actionState and myBookingId, or status 404 with Error code \"not_found\" when the session id does not exist.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Scheduled sessions with capacity 20 and bookedCount 14, capacity 12 and bookedCount 10, capacity 12 and bookedCount 11, capacity 16 and bookedCount 16 with waitlistCount 3, and a Cancelled by studio session with capacity 20 and bookedCount 0","id":"AC-8.1","level":"api","then":"The availabilityLabel values returned are \"6 spots left\", \"Only 2 left\", \"1 spot left\", \"Full · 3 on waitlist\" and \"Cancelled\", and the capacityLabel values are \"6 of 20 spots left\", \"2 of 12 spots left\", \"1 of 12 spots left\", \"0 of 16 spots left\" and \"20 of 20 spots left\"","when":"A client reads each session via GET /api/sessions/{id}"}],"ears":"The Booking API shall set each session's capacityLabel to \"<spots left> of <capacity> spots left\" and its availabilityLabel to \"Cancelled\" for studio-cancelled sessions, \"Full · <waitlistCount> on waitlist\" when no spots are left, \"1 spot left\" for one spot, \"Only <n> left\" for two or three spots, and \"<n> spots left\" for four or more spots.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The injected clock reads 2026-10-14 10:00 London; the demo member holds Booked record 501 for a session starting at 11:30 London that day","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"The response actionState has kind \"booked\", canChange true, bookingId 501, lateCancellation true, and myBookingId is 501","when":"A client sends GET /api/sessions/{that id}"},{"given":"The demo member holds Waitlisted record 502 at position 2 for a full session starting tomorrow","id":"AC-9.2","level":"api","then":"The response actionState has kind \"waitlisted\", position 2, bookingId 502 and myBookingId is 502","when":"A client sends GET /api/sessions/{that id}"},{"given":"A session starting tomorrow with capacity 12 and bookedCount 10 and no demo record, and a full session starting tomorrow with waitlistCount 3 and no demo record","id":"AC-9.3","level":"api","then":"The first response actionState is kind \"book\" with spotsLeft 2 and myBookingId null; the second is kind \"join_waitlist\" with position 4 and myBookingId null","when":"A client reads both sessions"},{"given":"The demo member holds a Booked record for a session that started 10 minutes ago and has not ended","id":"AC-9.4","level":"api","then":"The response actionState has kind \"booked\" and canChange false","when":"A client reads that session"}],"ears":"The Booking API shall set each session's actionState and myBookingId for the demo member as: booked (bookingId, lateCancellation true when under 2 hours to start) when holding a Booked record, waitlisted (position) when holding a Waitlisted record, book (spotsLeft) when spots remain, and join_waitlist (position = waitlistCount + 1) when full, with canChange false once the class has started.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The injected clock reads 2026-10-14 10:00 London and four Scheduled sessions start at 2026-10-21 10:01, 2026-10-14 10:10, 2026-10-14 09:30 London, plus one Cancelled by studio session tomorrow","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"Each response actionState has kind \"disabled\" and canChange false, with reason values \"Booking opens 7 days before class\", \"Booking closes 15 minutes before class\", \"Class has started\" and \"Cancelled by studio\" respectively","when":"A client reads each session via GET /api/sessions/{id}"}],"ears":"While the demo member holds no Booked or Waitlisted record for a session that is studio-cancelled, started, more than 7 days ahead, or under 15 minutes from start, the Booking API shall return that session's actionState with kind \"disabled\", canChange false and reason \"Cancelled by studio\", \"Class has started\", \"Booking opens 7 days before class\" or \"Booking closes 15 minutes before class\" respectively.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","ASM-13","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The injected clock reads 2026-10-14 07:42 London and session 102 \"Reformer Core\" starts Wed 2026-10-14 09:30 London with capacity 12 and bookedCount 10","id":"AC-11.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201; booking.status is \"Booked\", booking.lateCancel is false, booking.cancelledAt is null; session.bookedCount is 11, session.availabilityLabel is \"1 spot left\", session.actionState.kind is \"booked\"; message is \"You're booked for Reformer Core · Wed 09:30\"","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings with body {\"sessionId\":102}"},{"given":"The booking from AC-11.1 was created","id":"AC-11.2","level":"api","then":"The response upcoming list contains a row for session 102 with status \"Booked\" and badge \"Booked\", and a bookings row exists in the SQLite database","when":"A client sends GET /api/me/bookings"}],"ears":"When createBooking succeeds for a session, the Booking API shall store a Booked record for the demo member and return status 201 with a BookingChange whose booking has status Booked, whose session shows bookedCount increased by 1 and actionState booked, and whose message is \"You're booked for <name> · <Ddd HH:mm>\" in Europe/London time.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","I-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A session starting tomorrow with capacity 16, bookedCount 16 and waitlistCount 2","id":"AC-12.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409, code is \"class_full\", session.actionState.kind is \"join_waitlist\" with position 3, and the count of the demo member's records for that session is 0","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings for it"}],"ears":"If createBooking targets a session with no spots left, then the Booking API shall return status 409 with Error code \"class_full\" and the refreshed session in the error's session field, without storing a record.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The injected clock reads 2026-10-14 10:00 London; sessions with spots left start at 2026-10-21 10:01 and 2026-10-14 10:14 London","id":"AC-13.1","level":"api","then":"Both responses have status 409 and code \"outside_booking_window\"","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings for each"},{"given":"The same clock; sessions with spots left start at exactly 2026-10-21 10:00 and exactly 2026-10-14 10:15 London","id":"AC-13.2","level":"api","then":"Both responses have status 201","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings for each"},{"given":"The same clock; a session started at 09:30 London today and a Cancelled by studio session tomorrow, both with spots left","id":"AC-13.3","level":"api","then":"The responses have status 409 with codes \"class_has_started\" and \"cancelled_by_studio\" respectively, and no record is stored for either","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings for each"}],"ears":"If createBooking targets a session that is studio-cancelled, has started, starts more than 7 days from now or starts less than 15 minutes from now, then the Booking API shall return status 409 with Error code \"cancelled_by_studio\", \"class_has_started\" or \"outside_booking_window\" respectively, without storing a record.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-13","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The demo member holds Booked \"Power HIIT\" tomorrow 18:00–18:45 London","id":"AC-14.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409, code is \"overlap\" and message is \"You're already booked for Power HIIT at 18:00–18:45.\"","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings for a Spin session tomorrow 18:30–19:15 with spots left"},{"given":"The same Booked \"Power HIIT\" tomorrow 18:00–18:45","id":"AC-14.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings for a session tomorrow starting exactly 18:45"}],"ears":"If createBooking targets a session whose time range overlaps a session the demo member holds as Booked, then the Booking API shall return status 409 with Error code \"overlap\" and message \"You're already booked for <name> at <HH:mm>–<HH:mm>.\" naming the conflicting class in Europe/London time.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The demo member holds 10 Booked records for non-overlapping classes that have not started","id":"AC-15.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409, code is \"limit_reached\", message is \"You've reached the limit of 10 upcoming classes.\" and the count of Booked rows stays 10","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings for an 11th non-overlapping session with spots left"},{"given":"The demo member holds 9 such Booked records","id":"AC-15.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings for a 10th non-overlapping session"}],"ears":"If createBooking is requested while the demo member already holds 10 Booked records for classes that have not started, then the Booking API shall return status 409 with Error code \"limit_reached\" and message \"You've reached the limit of 10 upcoming classes.\"","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A session starting tomorrow with spots left and no demo record","id":"AC-16.1","level":"api","then":"The first response status is 201, the second response status is 409 with code \"already_booked\", and the count of Booked rows for that session and member is 1","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings for it twice in a row"},{"given":"The demo member holds a Waitlisted record for a full session","id":"AC-16.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with code \"already_booked\"","when":"A client sends POST /api/waitlist for that session"},{"given":"The demo member booked a session and then cancelled it","id":"AC-16.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201, the returned booking id differs from the cancelled one, and the database has 2 rows for that session and member (one Cancelled, one Booked)","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings for that session again"}],"ears":"If createBooking or joinWaitlist targets a session for which the demo member already holds a Booked or Waitlisted record, then the Booking API shall return status 409 with Error code \"already_booked\", checked in the same database transaction as the insert, while Cancelled records do not block a new record.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-6","ASM-8","ASM-16"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API is running","id":"AC-17.1","level":"api","then":"Both response statuses are 400 with code \"invalid_request\"","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings with body {} and POST /api/waitlist with body {\"sessionId\":\"abc\"}"},{"given":"No session with id 99999 exists","id":"AC-17.2","level":"api","then":"Both response statuses are 404 with code \"not_found\"","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings and POST /api/waitlist with body {\"sessionId\":99999}"}],"ears":"If createBooking or joinWaitlist receives a body without an integer sessionId, then the Booking API shall return status 400 with Error code \"invalid_request\", and for an unknown sessionId status 404 with Error code \"not_found\".","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The demo member created Booked record B for \"Reformer Core\" (bookedCount 10 → 11) and the injected clock has advanced 5 seconds","id":"AC-18.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, message is \"Booking undone — Reformer Core\", session.bookedCount is 10, session.myBookingId is null, and no row with id B remains in the database","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings/{B}/undo"},{"given":"Booked record B was created and the injected clock has advanced 6 seconds","id":"AC-18.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409, code is \"undo_expired\", and row B still has status Booked","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings/{B}/undo"},{"given":"The demo member holds Waitlisted record W created 1 second ago, and no record 99999 exists","id":"AC-18.3","level":"api","then":"The responses have status 409 with code \"invalid_booking_state\" and status 404 with code \"not_found\" respectively","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings/{W}/undo and POST /api/bookings/99999/undo"}],"ears":"When undoBooking is called for a Booked record created no more than 5 seconds earlier, the Booking API shall delete that record and return status 200 with an UndoResult whose session shows the restored counts and whose message is \"Booking undone — <name>\", returning 409 \"undo_expired\" after 5 seconds, 409 \"invalid_booking_state\" for a record that is not Booked, and 404 \"not_found\" for an unknown id.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","Q-1","ASM-13","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The injected clock reads 2026-10-14 17:30 London and the demo member holds Booked record 506 for \"Power Spin\" starting 19:00 London that day","id":"AC-19.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200; booking.status is \"Cancelled\", booking.lateCancel is true, booking.cancelledAt is 2026-10-14T16:30:00Z; message starts with \"Booking cancelled — Power Spin\"","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings/506/cancel"},{"given":"The injected clock is exactly 2 hours before the start of a session the demo member holds as Booked","id":"AC-19.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and booking.lateCancel is false","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings/{id}/cancel"},{"given":"A Cancelled record C, a Booked record S whose class started 5 minutes ago, and no record 99999","id":"AC-19.3","level":"api","then":"The responses are status 409 code \"invalid_booking_state\", status 409 code \"class_has_started\", and status 404 code \"not_found\" respectively, and row S still has status Booked","when":"A client cancels C, S and 99999"}],"ears":"When cancelBooking is called for a Booked record whose class has not started, the Booking API shall set the record to Cancelled with cancelledAt set to now and lateCancel true only when less than 2 hours remain before start, and return status 200 with a BookingChange whose message begins \"Booking cancelled — <name>\", returning 409 \"invalid_booking_state\" for a non-Booked record, 409 \"class_has_started\" after start, and 404 \"not_found\" for an unknown id.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","ASM-13","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A session starting tomorrow with capacity 10, bookedCount 10 (including the demo member's Booked record) and waitlistCount 2","id":"AC-20.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, session.bookedCount is 10, session.waitlistCount is 1 and session.availabilityLabel is \"Full · 1 on waitlist\"","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings/{demo record}/cancel"},{"given":"A session starting tomorrow with capacity 20, bookedCount 19 including the demo member and waitlistCount 0","id":"AC-20.2","level":"api","then":"The response session.bookedCount is 18 and session.waitlistCount is 0","when":"A client cancels the demo member's record"}],"ears":"When the demo member cancels a Booked record for a session whose waitlistCount is above 0, the Booking API shall promote the first anonymous waitlisted member by lowering the session's waitlistCount by 1 and keeping bookedCount unchanged, and when the waitlist is empty it shall lower bookedCount by 1.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Session 103 \"HIIT Blast\" starts Wed 2026-10-14 12:15 London with capacity 16, bookedCount 16 and waitlistCount 3; the injected clock reads 2026-10-14 08:50 London","id":"AC-21.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201; booking.status is \"Waitlisted\" and booking.waitlistPosition is 4; session.waitlistCount is 4, session.availabilityLabel is \"Full · 4 on waitlist\", session.actionState is kind \"waitlisted\" with position 4; message is \"You're on the waitlist for HIIT Blast · Wed 12:15 — you're #4\"","when":"A client sends POST /api/waitlist with body {\"sessionId\":103}"}],"ears":"When joinWaitlist succeeds for a full session, the Booking API shall store a Waitlisted record with waitlistPosition equal to the previous waitlistCount plus 1 and return status 201 with a BookingChange whose session shows waitlistCount increased by 1 and actionState waitlisted, and whose message is \"You're on the waitlist for <name> · <Ddd HH:mm> — you're #<position>\".","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The injected clock reads 2026-10-14 10:00 London; a session tomorrow with 2 spots left; full sessions that are Cancelled by studio, started at 09:30 today, start at 2026-10-21 10:01, and start at 10:10 today","id":"AC-22.1","level":"api","then":"The responses all have status 409 with codes \"not_full\", \"cancelled_by_studio\", \"class_has_started\", \"outside_booking_window\" and \"outside_booking_window\" respectively, and the count of Waitlisted rows for the demo member does not change","when":"A client sends POST /api/waitlist for each"}],"ears":"If joinWaitlist targets a session that still has spots, is studio-cancelled, has started, or is outside the 7-day / 15-minute booking window, then the Booking API shall return status 409 with Error code \"not_full\", \"cancelled_by_studio\", \"class_has_started\" or \"outside_booking_window\" respectively, without storing a record.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The demo member holds Waitlisted record 504 at position 2 for \"Vinyasa Flow\" starting in 30 minutes, with waitlistCount 3","id":"AC-23.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200; booking.status is \"Cancelled\", booking.lateCancel is false, booking.cancelledAt is not null, booking.waitlistPosition is null; session.waitlistCount is 2, session.actionState.kind is \"join_waitlist\" with position 3; message is \"You've left the waitlist for Vinyasa Flow\"","when":"A client sends POST /api/bookings/504/leave-waitlist"},{"given":"A Booked record K, a Waitlisted record P whose class started 5 minutes ago, and no record 99999","id":"AC-23.2","level":"api","then":"The responses are status 409 code \"invalid_booking_state\", status 409 code \"class_has_started\", and status 404 code \"not_found\" respectively","when":"A client sends leave-waitlist for K, P and 99999"}],"ears":"When leaveWaitlist is called for a Waitlisted record whose class has not started, the Booking API shall set the record to Cancelled with lateCancel false and cancelledAt set to now, lower the session's waitlistCount by 1, and return status 200 with message \"You've left the waitlist for <name>\", returning 409 \"invalid_booking_state\" for a non-Waitlisted record, 409 \"class_has_started\" after start, and 404 \"not_found\" for an unknown id.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Session 105 is full with capacity 14, bookedCount 14, waitlistCount 2, and the demo member holds Waitlisted record 502 at position 1","id":"AC-24.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200; booking.id is 502, booking.status is \"Booked\", booking.waitlistPosition is null; session.bookedCount is 14, session.waitlistCount is 1, session.actionState.kind is \"booked\"; the database row 502 has a non-null promoted-at value","when":"A client sends POST /api/test/sessions/105/simulate-other-member-cancellation"},{"given":"A full session with waitlistCount 4 where the demo member holds a Waitlisted record at position 3","id":"AC-24.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200; booking.status is \"Waitlisted\" and booking.waitlistPosition is 2; session.waitlistCount is 3","when":"A client calls the simulate hook for it"},{"given":"A session with capacity 14, bookedCount 12 and waitlistCount 0, with no demo record","id":"AC-24.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, booking is null and session.bookedCount is 11","when":"A client calls the simulate hook for it"},{"given":"The demo member is first on the waitlist for a session that overlaps a class they already hold as Booked","id":"AC-24.4","level":"api","then":"The response booking.status is \"Booked\" and booking.skipReason is null","when":"A client calls the simulate hook for that session"},{"given":"No session with id 99999 exists","id":"AC-24.5","level":"api","then":"The response status is 404 with code \"not_found\"","when":"A client sends POST /api/test/sessions/99999/simulate-other-member-cancellation"}],"ears":"When simulateOtherMemberCancellation is called for a session, the Booking API shall promote the demo member to Booked (clearing waitlistPosition and recording promoted-at) when they are first on the waitlist, otherwise lower waitlistCount by 1 and move the demo member's waitlist position up by 1 when the waitlist is not empty, otherwise lower bookedCount by 1, and return status 200 with the session and the demo member's affected booking (null when they held no Waitlisted record), or 404 \"not_found\" for an unknown session.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","Q-3","Q-4","Q-7","ASM-5","ASM-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The injected clock reads 2026-10-14 10:00 London; the demo member holds Booked for today 19:00, Waitlisted position 2 for tomorrow 07:00, Booked for Fri 2026-10-16 18:15, a Booked record whose class ended on 2026-10-10, a late-Cancelled record for a class on 2026-10-08, and a Booked record for a Cancelled by studio session tomorrow","id":"AC-25.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200; upcoming has groups labelled \"Today\", \"Tomorrow\" and \"Fri 16 Oct\" in that order, with badges \"Booked\", \"Waitlisted #2\" and \"Booked\"; past lists the 2026-10-10 row with badge \"Attended\" before the 2026-10-08 row with badge \"Late cancel\"; the row for the studio-cancelled session has status and badge \"Cancelled by studio\"","when":"A client sends GET /api/me/bookings"},{"given":"The injected clock reads 2026-10-14 17:30 London and the demo member holds Booked for 19:00 that day and Booked for 2026-10-16 18:15","id":"AC-25.2","level":"api","then":"The 19:00 row has isLateIfCancelledNow true and canChange true; the 2026-10-16 row has isLateIfCancelledNow false","when":"A client sends GET /api/me/bookings"}],"ears":"When a client calls getMyBookings, the Booking API shall return the demo member's Booked and Waitlisted records for classes that have not ended under upcoming, grouped by Europe/London day labelled \"Today\", \"Tomorrow\" or \"Ddd d Mon\" and ordered by start time, and their Attended and Cancelled records under past ordered by most recent start first, each row carrying the contract badge (Booked, Waitlisted #N, Attended, Cancelled, Late cancel, Cancelled by studio).","id":"REQ-25","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The demo member holds a Booked record for a class whose end time has just passed on the injected clock","id":"AC-26.1","level":"api","then":"The record appears in the past list with status \"Attended\", badge \"Attended\" and canChange false, and the database row's stored status value is still Booked","when":"A client sends GET /api/me/bookings"}],"ears":"While a Booked record's class has ended, the Booking API shall report that record with status \"Attended\", badge \"Attended\" and canChange false in every response, without changing the stored status.","id":"REQ-26","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The injected clock reads 2026-10-14 10:00 London; the demo member has ended Booked records on 2026-09-30, 2026-10-06, 2026-10-10 and 2026-10-13, a Cancelled record on 2026-10-07, 2 Booked records for future classes and 1 Waitlisted record","id":"AC-27.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 with upcoming 2, classesThisMonth 3 and currentStreakWeeks 3","when":"A client sends GET /api/me/stats"},{"given":"The injected clock reads 2026-10-14 10:00 London; the demo member's only ended Booked records are on 2026-10-06 and 2026-09-29","id":"AC-27.2","level":"api","then":"The response currentStreakWeeks value is 2 and classesThisMonth is 1","when":"A client sends GET /api/me/stats"}],"ears":"When a client calls getStats, the Booking API shall return upcoming as the count of Booked records for classes not yet started, classesThisMonth as the count of Attended records in the current Europe/London calendar month, and currentStreakWeeks as the number of consecutive Monday-to-Sunday London weeks with at least one Attended record counted back from the current week, starting from the previous week when the current week has none.","id":"REQ-27","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","Q-2","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The demo member was promoted by the simulate hook into \"Power Ride\" starting Thu 2026-10-15 07:15 London","id":"AC-28.1","level":"api","then":"Both responses have status 200 and a notices list with 1 item whose message is \"Good news! You're off the waitlist and booked for Power Ride · Thu 07:15\"","when":"A client sends GET /api/me/promotion-notices twice"},{"given":"The notice from AC-28.1 is listed","id":"AC-28.2","level":"api","then":"The first response status is 204 with an empty body, the second response notices list is empty, and the booking row has a non-null notice-acknowledged value","when":"A client sends POST /api/me/promotion-notices/acknowledge and then GET /api/me/promotion-notices"}],"ears":"When a client calls listPromotionNotices, the Booking API shall return one notice per promoted booking whose notice is not yet acknowledged, with bookingId, sessionId, sessionName, startsAt and message \"Good news! You're off the waitlist and booked for <name> · <Ddd HH:mm>\", and acknowledgePromotionNotices shall be answered with status 204 after marking all current notices acknowledged.","id":"REQ-28","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","Q-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API is configured with a SQLite connection string pointing at a database file whose tables have been dropped","id":"AC-29.1","level":"api","then":"Both response statuses are 500, the body field code is \"storage_failure\", and the response body contains neither \"Exception\" nor \"   at \"","when":"A client sends GET /api/me/bookings and POST /api/bookings with a valid body"}],"ears":"If reading or writing the SQLite database fails or any other exception is not handled, then the Booking API shall return status 500 with Error code \"storage_failure\" and a plain-language message, with no exception type or stack trace in the body.","id":"REQ-29","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The connection string points at a SQLite file that does not exist","id":"AC-30.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the sessions list is not empty","when":"The app starts via WebApplicationFactory and a client sends GET /api/schedule"},{"given":"The app has started once and a client created a booking","id":"AC-30.2","level":"api","then":"The response still contains the created booking and the count of session rows equals the count before the restart","when":"The app is restarted on the same database file and a client sends GET /api/me/bookings"},{"given":"A clean checkout with no app.db file","id":"AC-30.3","level":"job","then":"No app.db file exists afterwards in the App.Api folder or its build output","when":"dotnet build runs and writes App.Api/openapi/built.json"}],"anchors":[{"lineEnd":6,"lineStart":5,"path":"App.Api/Program.cs","quote":"builder.Services.AddOpenApi();\n// a local file database; nothing touches it at startup (the build runs this file to write the API's OpenAPI document)"}],"ears":"When the application starts normally and its SQLite database has no data, the Booking API shall create the schema with EnsureCreated and insert the sample data, skipping both steps when it is run by the build to generate the OpenAPI document and leaving an already populated database unchanged.","id":"REQ-30","op":"MODIFIED","sources":["I-2","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A freshly seeded database with the injected clock at the seeding time","id":"AC-31.1","level":"api","then":"The session row count is between 1 and 15; the schedule response for today has at least 1 session; across the current and next week the returned sessions include one with availabilityLabel starting \"Full · \" and waitlistCount at least 1 and one with status \"Cancelled by studio\"; the bookings response upcoming list has at least one \"Booked\" and one \"Waitlisted #\" badge and the past list has at least one \"Attended\" row; stats upcoming is at least 1","when":"A client sends GET /api/schedule, GET /api/me/bookings and GET /api/me/stats, and a test counts session rows"}],"ears":"When the sample data is inserted, the Booking API shall create at most 15 sessions dated relative to the Europe/London day of seeding, including at least one Scheduled session that day, one full session with a waitlist, one Cancelled by studio session, and for the demo member at least one upcoming Booked record, one Waitlisted record and one Booked record for a class that has already ended.","id":"REQ-31","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","Q-8","ASM-4"]}],"suggestions":["Update the contract description that says the API runs in the browser over local storage, through the contract-change process, since this run uses SQLite (ASM-10).","Decide whether promotion should be skipped with a skipReason (overlap, limit_reached, outside_booking_window), since the contract defines SkipReason but ASM-15 promotes anyway.","Add a unique partial index on (member, session) for Booked/Waitlisted rows to protect against concurrent duplicate taps, beyond the in-transaction check (ASM-16).","Settle the ASM-1 vs ASM-11 conflict over path mapping explicitly in the assumptions artifact.","Consider limiting the /test simulate hook to non-production environments in a later release (Q-3 keeps it mapped everywhere)."]}],"models":["claude-opus-5-5","claude-opus-5-5","claude-opus-5-5"],"notes":["No OpenAI key: specify-other ran on claude-opus-5-5 (same family as the implementer)"]}